{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJW1r6nHXaqoay16NQfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":18075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":952,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae916214-4f79-4252-8435-cffb906369c3","uuid":"2397e19c-b5a6-4d96-b3e0-3fc52ccc71fb","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:35.061Z","request_id":"req_011CgJW1qmBWiog5WgAQiV7k","thinking_duration_ms":65352,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJW1r6nHXaqoay16NQfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BafCZW5Abw21bmqV8ZwYVy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat board.md; cat > answer.md <<'E'\n# Answer\n\n1. A stable set exists **iff K is even**.\n2. For K = 2m the stable set is **unique**: V = {(0,m,m), (m,0,m), (m,m,0)}. For odd K there is none.\n\n(Confirmed by exhaustive search for K = 2..9, `enum.py`: exactly one stable set for even K, none for odd K.)\n\n## Proof\n\nNotation: x dominates y iff x_i>y_i for at least two coordinates i. So **y is not dominated by x iff x_i ≤ y_i for at least two coordinates**.\n\n**Lemma 1 (internal stability).** For distinct allocations x,y: neither dominates the other iff x_i=y_i for some i.\nIf x_i=y_i, then x dominating y would need both other coordinates larger, which contradicts equal sums. Likewise y cannot dominate x. Conversely, suppose x and y agree nowhere. Two coordinates have the same sign of x_i−y_i, and the three differences sum to 0 with none zero. So some two coordinates have the same sign, and that sign is either + (x dominates y) or − (y dominates x).\nSo V is internally stable iff any two elements agree in some coordinate. Distinct allocations agree in exactly one coordinate (agreeing in two forces the third by the sum).\n\n**Existence for even K=2m.** V={(0,m,m),(m,0,m),(m,m,0)} is pairwise agreeing (each pair shares an m in the same position), so it is internally stable. If y=(a,b,c)∉V, then at most one coordinate of y is ≥m. Otherwise two coordinates are ≥m, they sum to ≥2m=K, so they equal m, the third is 0, and y∈V. Say a,b<m. Then (m,m,0) has two coordinates larger than y's (a<m, b<m), so it dominates y. The other cases are symmetric, so V is externally stable.\n\n**Any stable set V (K≥2) equals this set, so K is even.** V is nonempty (a nonempty point set is not externally stable if V is empty).\n\n*Case A: V is a star, i.e. all elements have the same value c in some coordinate, say x_1=c (other coordinates symmetric).*\nNo two points of the line L={x_1=c} dominate each other (Lemma 1), so every point of L not in V would have to be dominated by a point of V⊆L. That cannot happen, so L⊆V, hence V=L.\n- If c<K, take y=(c+1,y2,y3) with y2+y3=K−c−1. A point x∈L dominates y only if x2>y2 and x3>y3, since x1=c<y1. That needs x2+x3 ≥ y2+y3+2 = K−c+1, but x2+x3=K−c. So y∉V is undominated, contradiction.\n- If c=K, then V={(K,0,0)} and (0,K,0) is undominated and not in V, contradiction.\n\n*Case B: V is not a star in any coordinate.* |V|≥2, since one point is a star. Take distinct x,y∈V; they agree in exactly one coordinate, WLOG coordinate 1: x=(a,b,c), y=(a,b',c') with b≠b', c≠c'. Since V is not a star in coordinate 1, some z∈V has z_1≠a. z agrees with x in coordinate 2 or 3 and with y in coordinate 2 or 3, and not in the same coordinate (x,y differ there). By symmetry (swap players 2,3) take z_2=b and z_3=c'. So z=(e,b,c') with e≠a.\nNow let w∈V be any element.\n- If w_1=a: w agrees with z in coordinate 2 or 3, so w=x (w_2=b) or w=y (w_3=c').\n- If w_1≠a: w agrees with x in coordinate 2 or 3, and with y in coordinate 2 or 3, not in the same one. So w=z (w_2=b, w_3=c') or w=u=(·,b',c) (w_2=b', w_3=c). In the second case u must agree with z, and u_2=b'≠b, u_3=c≠c', so u_1=z_1. Using sums, a+b+c=a+b'+c' gives b+c=b'+c', and e+b+c'=e+b'+c gives b+c'=b'+c. Subtracting these gives c=c' and then b=b', a contradiction.\n\nHence V={x,y,z} with x=(p,q,K−p−q), y=(p,K−p−r,r), z=(K−q−r,q,r), where p=x_1=y_1, q=x_2=z_2, r=y_3=z_3, and all coordinates are ≥0.\nLet s=K−p−q−r. Then x=(p,q,r+s), y=(p,q+s,r), z=(p+s,q,r). These are distinct, so s≠0.\n\nTake any w ≥ (p,q,r) componentwise with sum K. Then w≥x in coordinates 1,2, w≥y in coordinates 1,3, and w≥z in coordinates 2,3. So w is undominated by V. Such w are exactly (p,q,r)+(nonneg vector of total s), if s>0.\n- s≥2: there are C(s+2,2)≥6 such w, but at most 3 lie in V. So some w∉V is undominated, contradiction.\n- s=1: p+q+r=K−1≥1. If r≥1, w=(p+1,q+1,r−1) is ≥x,y,z in coordinates 1,2 (x=(p,q,r+1), y=(p,q+1,r), z=(p+1,q,r)), and w∉V because w_3=r−1 differs from the third coordinates r+1, r, r of x,y,z. If p≥1, w=(p−1,q+1,r+1) is ≥x,y,z in coordinates 2,3 and w_1=p−1∉{p,p,p+1}. If q≥1, w=(p+1,q−1,r+1) is ≥x,y,z in coordinates 1,3 and w_2=q−1∉{q,q+1,q}. In each case w is an undominated allocation outside V, a contradiction.\n- s=−t<0 (t≥1): the coordinates are x=(p,q,r−t), y=(p,q−t,r), z=(p−t,q,r), with p,q,r≥t. Any w with w_2≥q and w_3≥r is ≥x,y,z in coordinates 2,3, so it is undominated. Such w have w_1 ≤ K−q−r = p−t. If p>t, w=(p−t−1,q+1,r) is such a w. Its first coordinate p−t−1 differs from p, p, p−t, so w∉V. This is a contradiction, so p=t. Symmetrically (w_1≥p, w_3≥r gives q=t; w_1≥p, w_2≥q gives r=t). So p=q=r=t, K=p+q+r−t=2t, x=(t,t,0), y=(t,0,t), z=(0,t,t), which is the claimed set with m=t.\n\nSo every stable set equals {(0,m,m),(m,0,m),(m,m,0)} with K=2m. Odd K has no stable set, and for even K the stable set is unique. ∎\nE\necho \"[sonnet] 2026-10-23 answer.md written (even K unique set, odd none; full proof). FINAL\" >> board.md; touch SUBMIT"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":18075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":952,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae916214-4f79-4252-8435-cffb906369c3","uuid":"b065828a-72b8-4057-9822-08f30bc27eee","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:50.210Z","request_id":"req_011CgJW1qmBWiog5WgAQiV7k"}
